              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You will be given a full Elasticsearch search response JSON. For each element in hits.hits, read _source and return a normalized issues summary for the referenced item (by Item.ItemNumber). If any required attribute is missing or cannot be determined, set its value to \"Unknown\" exactly as spelled.\n\nFollow Instruction: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nFIELD MAPPING RULES\n- ItemNumber:\n  - From _source.Item.ItemNumber.\n  - If missing, \"Unknown\".\n\n- CompletenessScore:\n  - Use numeric score 1-100 if present in _source (e.g., _source.CompletenessScore or equivalent numeric field explicitly labeled as completeness). Do not infer.\n  - If not present, \"Unknown\".\n\n- QualityIssue:\n  - Source: _source.ItemLevelDataPresenceIndicator.QualityIssueFlag.\n  - Map \"Y\", \"y\"  ->\"Yes\".\n  - Map \"N\", \"n\" ->\"No\".\n  - If missing or any other value, \"Unknown\".\n\n- PendingCO:\n  - Source: _source.ItemLevelDataPresenceIndicator.PendingChangeFlag.\n  - Same mapping as QualityIssue (\"Y\"/true ->\"Yes\", \"N\"/false ->\"No\"). Else \"Unknown\".\n\n- Attachment:\n  - Source: _source.ItemRevisionVersion.RevisionLevelDataPresenceIndicator.ItemRevAttachmentsFlag.\n  - Map \"Y\", \"y\"  ->\"Present\".\n  - Map \"N\", \"n\" ->\"Missing\".\n  - If missing or any other value, \"Unknown\".\n\n- AlternateSupplier:\n  - Source: _source.ManufacturerItemRelation[*].MfgRelationshipStatus.\n  - If BOTH values \"ORA_ALTERNATE\" AND \"ORA_PREFERRED\" appear among any entries ->\"Yes\".\n  - If ManufacturerItemRelation is present but one or both of those values are missing ->\"No\".\n  - If ManufacturerItemRelation is entirely missing or empty ->\"Unknown\".\n\nPRIORITY RULES\nDefine issueCount as the number of undesirable states among:\n  - QualityIssue == \"Yes\"\n  - PendingCO == \"Yes\"\n  - Attachment == \"Missing\"\n  - AlternateSupplier == \"No\"\n\"Unknown\" values do NOT increase issueCount.\n\nLet cs be the numeric CompletenessScore if present; if CompletenessScore == \"Unknown\", use cs = 50 only for the purpose of priority calculation (do not output 50; still output \"Unknown\" in the field).\n\nAssign Priority as:\n  - Critical: issueCount >= 4 OR cs < 20\n  - High: issueCount == 3 OR (20 <= cs < 40)\n  - Medium: issueCount == 2 OR (40 <= cs < 70)\n  - Low: Otherwise\n\nCONSTRAINTS\n- Process every hit in hits.hits (zero or more).\n- Do not invent fields; do not infer CompletenessScore from any other metric.\n- All enum values must match exactly the allowed strings.\n- Return only the JSON object described in OUTPUT with the \"items\" array.\n\nINPUT\n {{$context.$nodes.GETITEMBASICINFOFORBOM.$output}}\n\nOUTPUT\n\n**Display a title \"BOM Data Gaps Impact Progress\"\n**Always include a concise text summary (1-2 sentences) that highlights the key insights, patterns, or takeaways from the visualization. Place this summary immediately before the information display.\n\nFor each item must show following columns:\n TITLE\n     - <Item number> - <Very short 2~3 words description>\n  SUMMARY\n      Details of attributes as below:\n      CompletenessScore: \"1-100 | Unknown\", QualityIssue : \"Yes | No | Unknown\", PendingCO: \"Yes | No | Unknown\", Attachment: \"Present | Missing | Unknown\",AlternateSupplier: \"Yes |No | Unknown\"\n\n BADGE TEXT (Severity)\n   Assign a single severity badge Strictly based on \"PRIORITY\": \n   - CRITICAL\n   - HIGH\n  - MEDIUM\n  - LOW\n\n  IMAGE: \n     Use ItemNumber to matching image url from {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACTCOMPONENTIMAGE.$output.result}} \n\nTIMESTAMP\nDO NOT Populate this."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
