        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "ExtractNPIItem"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770812557729"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACTNPIITEM",
          "id": "1770812473078",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770812473082_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "User text: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \n\nYou will be given arbitrary user text. Extract three fields and output exactly one JSON object with these keys and string values (in this order):\n{\n \"AttributeGroups\": \"...\",\n \"OrgCode\": \"...\",\n \"ItemNumber\": \"...\"\n}\n\nDefaults:\n- If a field is missing or invalid per its rules below, output \"-999\" for that field.\n\nGeneral parsing:\n- Case-insensitive for the phrase \"switch focus\" and for the AttributeGroups label.\n- Fields may include extra narration.\n- Be tolerant of punctuation and spacing variations.\n\nCore assumption for ItemNumber and OrgCode (no labels used):\n- The text will contain the phrase \"switch focus to\" (case-insensitive).\n- After this phrase, the **first value** before the next \",\" or the word \"and\" is the **ItemNumber**.\n- The **second value** (after a comma or the word \"and\") before the next \",\" or the word \"and\" is the **OrgCode**.\n- Example pattern: `Switch focus to SP-1003371, V1 and Attribute Groups Rohs,EUReach`\n  - ItemNumber = `SP-1003371`\n  - OrgCode = `V1`\n\nDetailed rules for ItemNumber and OrgCode:\n1) Find the phrase \"switch focus to\" (case-insensitive).\n2) From immediately after this phrase:\n   - Skip any extra spaces, commas, or the word \"and\".\n   - Read characters until the next comma \",\" or the standalone word \"and\"; trim spaces. This is the **ItemNumber candidate**.\n   - From after that separator, again skip spaces/commas/\"and\".\n   - Read characters until the next comma \",\" or the standalone word \"and\"; trim spaces. This is the **OrgCode candidate**.\n\nItemNumber validation:\n- Accept only candidates composed of alphanumerics, hyphens, or underscores: ^[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$.\n- INVALID candidates that MUST force ItemNumber to \"-999\":\n  - Any value containing a dot \".\" (e.g., \"1.2\")\n  - Any value in scientific notation: ^-?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?[eE][+-]?\\d+$\n  - No candidate was found after \"switch focus to\".\n- Preserve original casing. Do not truncate valid values.\n\nOrgCode extraction:\n- Take the OrgCode candidate found as the second value after \"switch focus to\" per the rules above.\n- Valid OrgCode must match ^[A-Za-z0-9]+$.\n- If no such candidate is found or it does not match this pattern, output \"-999\".\n\nAttributeGroups extraction (still label-based):\n- AttributeGroups must be explicitly labeled with one of (case-insensitive):\n  - \"Attribute Groups\", \"AttributeGroups\", \"Attribute Group\", \"AttributeGroup\".\n- Take the substring following the AttributeGroups label up to the next label (if any) or end of string.\n- Split into terms using:\n  - Commas \",\"\n  - The standalone word \"and\" (case-insensitive)\n- Do NOT split on generic whitespace; this preserves multi-word terms.\n- Remove empty entries and ignore entries that are purely numeric.\n- Preserve original spelling/casing and keep underscores/hyphens within terms.\n- Join the resulting terms with a single comma and no spaces. If none remain, output \"-999\".\n\nOutput:\n- Return only the single JSON object with exactly the keys \"AttributeGroups\", \"OrgCode\", \"ItemNumber\" in that order, and their string values. No extra text or fields.\n\nExamples:\n\n1) Input:\nSwitch focus to SP-1003371, V1 and Attribute Groups Rohs,EUReach\nOutput:\n{ \"AttributeGroups\": \"Rohs,EUReach\", \"OrgCode\": \"V1\", \"ItemNumber\": \"SP-1003371\" }\n\n2) Input (no Attribute Groups present):\nSwitch focus to SP-1003371 and V1\nOutput:\n{ \"AttributeGroups\": \"-999\", \"OrgCode\": \"V1\", \"ItemNumber\": \"SP-1003371\" }\n\n3) Input (invalid item, but valid org):\nSwitch focus to A1.2, V1 and Attribute Groups RoHS\nOutput:\n{ \"AttributeGroups\": \"RoHS\", \"OrgCode\": \"V1\", \"ItemNumber\": \"-999\" }\n\n4) Input (only item present):\nSwitch focus to SP-1003371\nOutput:\n{ \"AttributeGroups\": \"-999\", \"OrgCode\": \"-999\", \"ItemNumber\": \"SP-1003371\" }"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"AttributeGroups\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"OrgCode\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"ItemNumber\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
